.TH BODYHASH 1 "2026-11-11" "bodyhash 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bodyhash \- hash a file body, excluding marked regions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bodyhash
.BR hash | check | markers
.I FILE
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bodyhash
computes a hash of file content, excluding any regions delimited by
user-specified marker pairs. By default, it normalizes line endings, strips
UTF-8 BOM, and removes trailing whitespace to ensure consistent hashes
across different operating systems and editors.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B hash
Output the hash of the file body.
.TP
.B check
Compare the file body hash with an expected value. Exits 0 if they match, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.B markers
Display the line numbers where the specified markers are found.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exclude =\fISTART::END\fR
Exclude the block from \fISTART\fR to \fIEND\fR. Both lines are excluded.
This option can be used multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-algo =\fIALGO\fR
Specify the hash algorithm. Supported: \fBsha256\fR (default), \fBsha512\fR, \fBsha3-256\fR, \fBsha3-512\fR, \fBblake2b\fR, \fBblake2s\fR, \fBmd5\fR.
Algorithms other than sha256/md5/blake2b require \fBopenssl\fR to be installed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-normalize\-crlf
Do not convert CRLF/CR to LF. By default, line endings are normalized.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strip\-bom
Do not strip the UTF-8 BOM (Byte Order Mark) from the beginning of the file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strip\-trailing\-ws
Do not remove trailing whitespace from each line before hashing.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-trailing\-ws
Strip trailing whitespace (default).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strip\-leading\-ws
Keep leading whitespace (default).
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-leading\-ws
Remove leading whitespace from each line before hashing.
.TP
.B \-\-indent\-tabs=\fIN\fR
Replace tab characters with \fIN\fR spaces before hashing.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-preamble
Skip the content before the first START marker.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-epilogue
Skip the content after the last END marker.
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-start
Fail if the first START marker is not on line 1.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output (e.g., print OK on successful check).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all output except errors.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success (hash matched).
.TP
.B 1
Hash mismatch (check command only).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or marker order (end before start).
.TP
.B 3
Marker pair not found.
.TP
.B 4
File not found.
.TP
.B 5
Internal error (e.g., hasher produced no output).
.TP
.B 6
Unsupported algorithm, or algorithm requires missing \fBopenssl\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Hash the body of a C file, excluding the Doxygen header:
.EX
bodyhash hash file.c \-e '/**::*/'
.EE
.TP
Verify the hash against a known value:
.EX
bodyhash check file.c 1857616f15bd53f72c1733a1839421116c7bbb50579f2cdb9ceca9adfcd30fda \-e '/**::*/'
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sha256sum (1),
.BR openssl (1)
